@startuml

start

note

AGP Version (Android Gradle Plugin) :
Full name: Android Gradle Plugin
What it is: A Gradle plugin developed by Google that allows Gradle to understand and build Android apps.
Where it’s used: Declared in build.gradle (project-level or module-level) as:
id 'com.android.application' version '8.9.0'

Why it matters:
Controls the Android-specific build logic (generating APKs/AABs, resource merging, signing)
Must be compatible with Gradle version and Kotlin plugin version

Gradle Version :
Core build tool for Java, Kotlin, and Android.

Gradle Wrapper Version :
Ensures everyone builds the project using the same Gradle version.
android/gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.properties

Plugin Tools Version :
Examples:
com.android.application
org.jetbrains.kotlin.android
dev.flutter.flutter-gradle-plugin

Kotlin Version :
Declared in build.gradle or versions.gradle

Compatibility matrix :
https://docs.gradle.org/8.14.3/userguide/compatibility.html

Decision Workflow :
- Define Flutter Version
- Check compatible AGP version
- Use AGP version to define Gradle wrapper version
- Derive Kotlin version from AGP
- Derive JVM version from Gradle + AGP
- Define SDK version based on Flutter + AGP
- Define NDK version based on AGP

end note


:Define Flutter Version;
:Check Compatible AGP Version;
:Define Gradle Wrapper Version;
:Derive Kotlin Version;
:Derive JVM Version;
:Define SDK Version;
:Derive NDK Version;

note
AGP influences Gradle, Kotlin and NDK.
Flutter influences SDK.
end note


:Load DEVICE_IP from $HOME/.adb_device_ip;

if (DEVICE_IP file exists?) then (yes)
    :DEVICE_IP=$(cat $DEVICE_IP_FILE);
    :Print "Loaded device IP";
else (no)
    :Print "No saved device IP found";
endif


:Detect environment type;

if (WSL detected?) then (yes)
    :ENV_TYPE="WSL";
elseif (Windows detected?) then (yes)
    :ENV_TYPE="WINDOWS";
else (Linux)
    :ENV_TYPE="LINUX";
endif

:Print "Detected environment";


if (ENV_TYPE=="WSL") then (yes)
    :WIN_IP from /etc/resolv.conf;
    :export ADB_SERVER_SOCKET;
    :ADB_CMD="adb.exe";
else (no)
    :ADB_CMD="adb";
endif


:Parse arguments for FLUTTER_MODE and CLEAN_BUILD;
:Resolve PROJECT_ROOT;
:Print current directory;

:Run generate_local_properties.sh;


if (Running inside Docker?) then (yes)

    :Remove previous sdk.dir and ndk.dir;
    :Detect installed NDK version;

    if (NDK_VERSION found?) then (yes)
        :Write sdk.dir and ndk.dir;
    else (no)
        :Print "No NDK installation found";
        stop
    endif

    :Docker SDK + NDK paths configured;

endif


if (ENV_TYPE=="WSL") then (yes)
    :Ensure cmake.dir=/usr/bin;
endif


if (flutter command exists?) then (yes)
    :Flutter found;
else (no)
    :Flutter not found;
    stop
endif


:Fetch Flutter dependencies (flutter pub get);


if (CLEAN_BUILD==true) then (yes)
    :flutter clean;
endif


:Build APK;
:Locate APK;


if (APK exists?) then (yes)
    :Print APK path;
else (no)
    :APK not found;
    stop
endif


:Detect USB device;

if (USB device detected?) then (yes)
    :Enable TCP/IP mode;
endif


if (No device connected?) then (yes)
    :Reconnect using saved IP;
endif


if (Connected via Wi-Fi?) then (yes)
    :Print Wi-Fi connection;
else
    :Print USB connection;
endif


if (Device connected?) then (yes)

    :Install APK using adb;

    if (Install fails?) then (yes)
        :Uninstall and reinstall;
    endif

else (no)

    :No device connected, skipping install;

endif


stop

@enduml